---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import batteryInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/battery-upkeep-infographic.png";
import boostInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/boost-infographic.jpg";
import flashlightSafetyInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/flashlight-safety-infographic.jpg";
import flashlightsInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/flashlights-infographic.jpg";
import labelPrinterInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/label-printer-infographic.gif";
import safetyTipsInfographic from "../../assets/images/infographics/safety-tips-infographic.jpg";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Infographic &amp; Information Design | Kelp"
  description="Turn complex processes, research, and data into clear infographics for websites, campaigns, presentations, and social channels."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Content Creation Services"
    title="Infographics"
    description="When the information is valuable but hard to absorb, people tune out. We turn dense ideas, processes, and data into infographics that are easier to follow and easier to share."
    lottieFile="infographics.json"
  />
  <div class="wrapper infographics">
    <div
      class="infographics-grid"
      data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
      data-lg-reveal-stagger="0.1"
    >
      <h2>
        We Make
        <br /> Infographics Like...
      </h2>
      <Picture
        src={batteryInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="battery upkeep infographic"
        width={1700}
        height={5662}
        widths={[480, 900, 1700]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
      <Picture
        src={boostInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="marketing infographic"
        width={750}
        height={5945}
        widths={[360, 600, 750]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
      <Picture
        src={flashlightSafetyInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="flashlight safety infographic"
        width={600}
        height={1831}
        widths={[320, 480, 600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
      <Picture
        src={flashlightsInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="flashlights infographic"
        width={800}
        height={5020}
        widths={[400, 650, 800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
      <Picture
        src={labelPrinterInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="marketing infographic"
        width={600}
        height={1114}
        widths={[320, 480, 600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
      <Picture
        src={safetyTipsInfographic}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="safety tips infographic"
        width={600}
        height={3591}
        widths={[320, 480, 600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
        inferSize
      />
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes the information is strong, but the format is doing it no
        favors. Research, process explanations, educational content, and
        campaign messaging can become too dense for people to finish or
        remember.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the audience has to work too hard to understand the story, the
        message gets lost before the value lands.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We turn complex information into a clearer visual sequence, balancing
        copy, hierarchy, and design so people can understand the main point
        quickly and keep following the story.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Informational design</li>
        <li>Process visualization</li>
        <li>Explainers</li>
        <li>Flowcharts</li>
        <li>Tutorials</li>
        <li>Microcontent</li>
        <li>Social</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Find the Point Before Drawing the Chart</h2>
      <p>
        We identify the audience, the decision, and the one idea they should
        remember. Then we choose the right form: process diagram, comparison,
        timeline, map, data visualization, or step-by-step explainer. Accuracy
        matters as much as appearance, so we check labels, sources, and context
        before production.
      </p>
      <h2>Create Assets That Work Where People See Them</h2>
      <p>
        An infographic may need a full web version, a slide, a print piece, and
        smaller social excerpts. We plan the hierarchy for each setting so the
        information stays legible. Talk with Kelp about the story your data
        needs to tell.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        An infographic is useful when it makes a real relationship easier to
        understand: a process, comparison, timeline, or set of numbers. We start
        with the underlying information and the question the audience needs
        answered. The visual hierarchy follows that logic. For online use, we
        plan supporting text and accessible alternatives so the information can
        be understood beyond the image itself.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Process and workflow diagrams</li>
        <li>Data and comparison graphics</li>
        <li>Educational explainers</li>
        <li>Web, presentation, print, and social versions</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Share the underlying information and the decision the audience needs to
        make. We can recommend what should become a graphic and what should stay
        as text.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can you work with incomplete data?</h3>
      <p>
        We can help organize it, but we will mark gaps and avoid implying
        precision the source does not support.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Turn Your Info Into a Visual Story
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={85} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>

<style lang="scss" is:global>
  .infographics {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
    max-width: 1200px;
    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    &-grid {
      column-count: 2;
      column-gap: 2rem;
      picture {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
